<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Loot duties for motivated raids.

    These raiders are here for the food (or the valuables), NOT for a fight. They are thieves, and
    the whole point of the motivation is that a starvation raid reads differently from an assault:
    they walk in, take what they came for, and leave. They do not pick fights - not with a colonist
    standing next to them, not with one across the room. Hit them and they will fight back; leave
    them alone and they will rob you and go.

    Node order is the design. ThinkNode_Priority takes the first subnode that returns a job, so
    only what is above the loot node can beat looting:

      1. combat drugs (no aggression of its own, and every vanilla combat duty leads with it);
      2. HARMED RECENTLY -> fight back, out to 65 tiles, turrets included. This is the ONLY thing
         that makes them aggressive, and it is what the player controls: shoot them and they turn
         on you. Vanilla's Breaching duty uses the same ThinkNode_HarmedRecently wrapper;
      3. loot;
      4. nothing left worth taking -> leave.

    Two earlier versions of this file got the balance wrong in opposite directions, both worth
    remembering:

      * a single fight node BELOW the loot node with a 20-tile radius - looting outranked fighting,
        so a raider being shot kept walking to the stockpile;
      * fixing that by adding an UNCONDITIONAL 12-tile fight node above the loot node, plus a
        65-tile one below it - which made them attack colonists on sight and turned every
        starvation raid back into an ordinary assault.

    There is deliberately no unprovoked-combat node now, and no fight node below the loot node
    either. A raider who has nothing left to steal leaves; they do not go looking for a fight on
    the way out.

    The other half of this lives in JobGiver_FDSteal: the Steal job it hands out carries an
    expiryInterval with checkOverrideOnExpire, so a steal already in progress is re-checked against
    this tree every two seconds instead of running to completion. Without that, the ordering above
    would only ever apply to raiders who happened to be between jobs.
  -->

  <DutyDef>
    <defName>FD_LootFood</defName>
    <alwaysShowWeapon>true</alwaysShowWeapon>
    <thinkNode Class="ThinkNode_Priority">
      <subNodes>
        <li Class="JobGiver_TakeCombatEnhancingDrug" />

        <li Class="ThinkNode_HarmedRecently">
          <thresholdTicks>600</thresholdTicks>
          <subNodes>
            <li Class="JobGiver_AIFightEnemies"> <!-- shot at: fight back. the only aggression here -->
              <targetAcquireRadius>65</targetAcquireRadius>
              <targetKeepRadius>72</targetKeepRadius>
              <needLOSToAcquireNonPawnTargets>true</needLOSToAcquireNonPawnTargets>
              <allowTurrets>true</allowTurrets>
            </li>
          </subNodes>
        </li>

        <li Class="FactionDynamics.JobGiver_FDSteal">
          <lootCategory>Food</lootCategory>
          <searchRadius>9999</searchRadius>
        </li>

        <li Class="JobGiver_ExitMapBest">
          <defaultLocomotion>Jog</defaultLocomotion>
          <jobMaxDuration>200</jobMaxDuration>
          <forceCanDig>true</forceCanDig>
        </li>
      </subNodes>
    </thinkNode>
  </DutyDef>

  <DutyDef>
    <defName>FD_LootValuables</defName>
    <alwaysShowWeapon>true</alwaysShowWeapon>
    <thinkNode Class="ThinkNode_Priority">
      <subNodes>
        <li Class="JobGiver_TakeCombatEnhancingDrug" />

        <li Class="ThinkNode_HarmedRecently">
          <thresholdTicks>600</thresholdTicks>
          <subNodes>
            <li Class="JobGiver_AIFightEnemies"> <!-- shot at: fight back. the only aggression here -->
              <targetAcquireRadius>65</targetAcquireRadius>
              <targetKeepRadius>72</targetKeepRadius>
              <needLOSToAcquireNonPawnTargets>true</needLOSToAcquireNonPawnTargets>
              <allowTurrets>true</allowTurrets>
            </li>
          </subNodes>
        </li>

        <li Class="FactionDynamics.JobGiver_FDSteal">
          <lootCategory>Valuables</lootCategory>
          <searchRadius>9999</searchRadius>
        </li>

        <li Class="JobGiver_ExitMapBest">
          <defaultLocomotion>Jog</defaultLocomotion>
          <jobMaxDuration>200</jobMaxDuration>
          <forceCanDig>true</forceCanDig>
        </li>
      </subNodes>
    </thinkNode>
  </DutyDef>

</Defs>
